  showScore: 0
  dialogues:
  - character: {fileID: 11400000, guid: c8fcfa5882242b84b8bf1fb55659059e, type: 2}
    emotion: 0
    text: 'You hired a Bill of Quantities specialist who wrote the scopes of works
      for the ''problem'' packages, but all the other packages are reviewed with
      the in house team.

'
  - character: {fileID: 11400000, guid: c8fcfa5882242b84b8bf1fb55659059e, type: 2}
    emotion: 0
    text: Minor issues arise on a number of small packages. None of the activities
      are on the critical path (construction items on the programme which are required
      to be complete before the following construction can start). Your construction
      team moves items on the programme around. There are costs associated with the
      scope gaps themselves and delaying some smaller contractors completion dates,
      but the programme remains unaffected and the client is not alerted there has
      been an issue.
